            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Rams is a European trick-taking game family related to Nap and Loo, often played as a gambling or drinking game with optional entry into each hand.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Published rules appear in France around 1820, with related Austrian and Bavarian evidence from the same period and later spread to Sweden and America as Rounce.',
              },
            ],
          },
